                <pb facs="0964" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.5151/557: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-27T15:00:00-03:00">December 27, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 27—1:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. December import quotas for controlled exchange just announced total 303,000
                    pounds sterling. They include 12 countries but exclude not only the United
                    States but also Great Britain. Germany obtains largest quota, 100,000
                    pounds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
